{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>וזרעתיה</b> — that they multiply and fruitify like the seed of the land." "<b>ורחמתי את לא רוחמה</b> — these are the fathers." "<b>ואמרתי ללא עמי</b> — these are those born in their exile, and this prophecy is for the future. Or it is connected, the explanation being: if the exiles return from their evil way, they will return to their land. And do not wonder, saying: after HaShem decreed upon them that they stand in exile many years, how will they return?! For Jeremiah said concerning Jerusalem, 'it shall be given into the hand of the king of Babylon,' and He commands: do justice, and if you do so — the House will not be destroyed, and if you do not do so — it shall become a ruin."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "The phrase 'שלש שנים רבות' is taken as a conjoined idiom, 'many years,' though it reads hyper-literally as 'three, many years'; the sense is clearly the prolonged duration of the exile."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:01.200650096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}